  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* --- A bi-invariant metric on SU(2), and curvature from the bracket --- */\n/* ⟨X,Y⟩ = −2 tr(XY) makes the basis (E₁,E₂,E₃) orthonormal. */\nip(X, Y) := ratsimp( -2 * mat_trace(X . Y) )$\n\nprint(\"⟨X,Y⟩ = −2 tr(XY) on su(2):\")$\nprint(\"   Gram matrix = \",\n      genmatrix( lambda([i,j], ip(Eb[i], Eb[j])), 3, 3),\n      \"   orthonormal ✓\")$\n\n/* bi-invariance ⟺ ad_Z skew-adjoint */\nbad : 0$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:1 thru 3 do for k:1 thru 3 do\n  if ratsimp( ip(br(Eb[k], Eb[i]), Eb[j]) + ip(Eb[i], br(Eb[k], Eb[j])) ) # 0\n    then bad : bad + 1$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"bi-invariance test ⟨[Z,X],Y⟩ + ⟨X,[Z,Y]⟩ = 0 over all 27 triples:\")$\nprint(\"   violations = \", bad, \"   ⟹ the metric is bi-invariant.\")$\n\n/* sectional curvature straight from the bracket */\nsecK(X, Y) := ratsimp( (1/4)*ip(br(X,Y), br(X,Y))\n                       / ( ip(X,X)*ip(Y,Y) - ip(X,Y)^2 ) )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"K(X,Y) = ¼|[X,Y]|² / (|X|²|Y|² − ⟨X,Y⟩²) on basis pairs:\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:i+1 thru 3 do\n  print(\"   K(E\", i, \", E\", j, \") = \", secK(Eb[i], Eb[j]))$\n\n/* and for a GENERIC pair — constant curvature, not just on the basis */\nXg : x1*Eb[1] + x2*Eb[2] + x3*Eb[3]$\nYg : y1*Eb[1] + y2*Eb[2] + y3*Eb[3]$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   generic X = Σxᵢ Eᵢ, Y = Σyᵢ Eᵢ :  K = \", secK(Xg, Yg))$\nprint(\"   Constant, for every 2-plane at every point.  SU(2) with this\")$\nprint(\"   metric is a space form (4.07) — a round 3-sphere.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   Why ¼: [X,Y] corresponds to x × y under 5.01's hat map, and\")$\nprint(\"   |x×y|² = |x|²|y|² − (x·y)², so the numerator and denominator\")$\nprint(\"   cancel exactly, leaving ¼ with nothing left over.\")$\n\n/* which sphere? */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"K = 1/4 ⟹ radius 2, since K = 1/R² (3.04, 4.04).\")$\nprint(\"   Check against 4.05: S = n(n−1)K with n = 3 gives \", 3*2*(1/4),\n      \" for radius 2,\")$\nprint(\"   and rescaling the metric by ¼ gives K = 1 and S = \", 3*2*1,\n      \" — the value\")$\nprint(\"   4.05 computed for the unit 3-sphere by an entirely different route.\")$\n\n/* geodesics */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"∇_X Y = ½[X,Y] for a bi-invariant metric, so ∇_X X = ½[X,X] = \",\n      br(Eb[1], Eb[1]))$\nprint(\"Every left-invariant field is its own geodesic field: the\")$\nprint(\"ONE-PARAMETER SUBGROUPS ARE GEODESICS, and the group exponential\")$\nprint(\"of 5.02 coincides with the Riemannian exp_e of 4.03.\")$\nprint(\"   exp(t E₃) = \", ratsimp(matrixexp(t*Eb[3])),\n      \"  — a great circle on S³.\")$",
   "metadata": {},
