     "text": [
      "⟨X,Y⟩ = −2 tr(XY) on su(2):\n   Gram matrix =  matrix([1,0,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1])    orthonormal ✓\nbi-invariance test ⟨[Z,X],Y⟩ + ⟨X,[Z,Y]⟩ = 0 over all 27 triples:\n   violations =  0    ⟹ the metric is bi-invariant.\nK(X,Y) = ¼|[X,Y]|² / (|X|²|Y|² − ⟨X,Y⟩²) on basis pairs:\n   K(E 1 , E 2 ) =  1/4\n   K(E 1 , E 3 ) =  1/4\n   K(E 2 , E 3 ) =  1/4\n   generic X = Σxᵢ Eᵢ, Y = Σyᵢ Eᵢ :  K =  1/4\n   Constant, for every 2-plane at every point.  SU(2) with this\n   metric is a space form (4.07) — a round 3-sphere.\n   Why ¼: [X,Y] corresponds to x × y under 5.01's hat map, and\n   |x×y|² = |x|²|y|² − (x·y)², so the numerator and denominator\n   cancel exactly, leaving ¼ with nothing left over.\nK = 1/4 ⟹ radius 2, since K = 1/R² (3.04, 4.04).\n   Check against 4.05: S = n(n−1)K with n = 3 gives  3/2  for radius 2,\n   and rescaling the metric by ¼ gives K = 1 and S =  6  — the value\n   4.05 computed for the unit 3-sphere by an entirely different route.\n∇_X Y = ½[X,Y] for a bi-invariant metric, so ∇_X X = ½[X,X] =\n  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\nEvery left-invariant field is its own geodesic field: the\nONE-PARAMETER SUBGROUPS ARE GEODESICS, and the group exponential\nof 5.02 coincides with the Riemannian exp_e of 4.03.\nProviso: assuming 64*t # 0\n   exp(t E₃) =  matrix([%e^-((%i*t)/2),0],[0,%e^((%i*t)/2)])\n                 — a great circle on S³."
