  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": "/* --- Left-invariant but NOT bi-invariant: the ax+b group --- */\n/* Is there a bi-invariant inner product on aff(1)?  The condition is\n   ad_Zᵀ G + G ad_Z = 0 for every Z, a linear system in the entries of G. */\nadX : admat(Ab[1], Ab)$\nadY : admat(Ab[2], Ab)$\nGg  : matrix([pp, qq],[qq, rr])$\neqs : append( flatten(args( transpose(adX).Gg + Gg.adX )),\n              flatten(args( transpose(adY).Gg + Gg.adY )) )$\nprint(\"aff(1): ad_X = \", adX, \"   ad_Y = \", adY)$\nprint(\"   bi-invariance equations: \", eqs)$\nprint(\"   solution: \", linsolve(eqs, [pp, qq, rr]))$\nprint(\"   p = q = 0 forced, so G = diag(0, r): DEGENERATE.\")$\nprint(\"   No bi-invariant inner product on aff(1) is positive definite,\")$\nprint(\"   matching the degenerate Killing form found above.\")$\n\n/* --- but there is a left-invariant one, and it is the hyperbolic plane --- */\n/* Group: (a,b) with a > 0, acting on ℝ by x ↦ ax + b.\n   Product (a₀,b₀)·(a,b) = (a₀a, a₀b + b₀). */\nassume(a > 0, a0 > 0)$\ngL : matrix([1/a^2, 0],[0, 1/a^2])$        /* ds² = (da² + db²)/a² */\nJac : matrix([a0, 0],[0, a0])$             /* d of left translation */\ngAt : matrix([1/(a0*a)^2, 0],[0, 1/(a0*a)^2])$   /* g at the image point */\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"left translation L_{(a₀,b₀)}(a,b) = (a₀a, a₀b + b₀), Jacobian \", Jac)$\nprint(\"   pullback of g − g = \", ratsimp( transpose(Jac).gAt.Jac - gL ))$\nprint(\"   so ds² = (da² + db²)/a² is LEFT-invariant.\")$\nprint(\"   And that is the hyperbolic metric of 2.06 and 4.07, with (b,a)\")$\nprint(\"   the upper half-plane coordinates.\")$\n\n/* curvature, by Stage 4's machinery */\nts(e) := ratsimp(trigsimp(e))$\nchristoffel_hand(g, vars) := block([ginv, n_],\n  n_ : length(vars),  ginv : ratsimp(invert(g)),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( ginv[k][l]*( diff(g[j][l], vars[i]) + diff(g[i][l], vars[j])\n                        - diff(g[i][j], vars[l]) ), l, 1, n_)/2 ),\n    j,1,n_), i,1,n_), k,1,n_) )$\nriem_hand(g, vars) := block([G, n_],\n  G : christoffel_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( diff(G[l][j][k], vars[i]) - diff(G[l][i][k], vars[j])\n        + sum( G[l][i][m]*G[m][j][k] - G[l][j][m]*G[m][i][k], m, 1, n_) ),\n    k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_), l,1,n_) )$\nriem_low_hand(g, vars) := block([Rr, n_],\n  Rr : riem_hand(g, vars), n_ : length(vars),\n  makelist( makelist( makelist( makelist(\n    ts( sum( g[l][m]*Rr[m][i][j][k], m,1,n_) ),\n    l,1,n_), k,1,n_), j,1,n_), i,1,n_) )$\nK2d(g, vars) := block([Rm], Rm : riem_low_hand(g, vars),\n  ts( Rm[1][2][2][1] / determinant(g) ) )$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   K = \", K2d(gL, [a, b]), \"   — the hyperbolic plane, K = −1 ✓\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"A bi-invariant metric forces K = ¼|[X,Y]|²/(...) ≥ 0.  Here K = −1,\")$\nprint(\"so this left-invariant metric CANNOT be bi-invariant — which the\")$\nprint(\"linear system above already showed directly.  Three independent\")$\nprint(\"routes to the same fact:\")$\nprint(\"   • the Killing form of aff(1) is degenerate\")$\nprint(\"   • the bi-invariance equations force a degenerate G\")$\nprint(\"   • the curvature is negative, and bi-invariant ⟹ K ≥ 0\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"So the hyperbolic plane is a LIE GROUP with a left-invariant metric,\")$\nprint(\"as well as the homogeneous space PSL₂(ℝ)/SO(2).  Two descriptions of\")$\nprint(\"the same surface, and 2.06 used neither.\")$",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 4,
   "outputs": [
    {
